    "title": "Cheese Board Breaks Out As Berkeley Icon Finally Grabs Next Door - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Eileen Vargas ,\n7 hours ago After an eight-year wait and a lot of side-eye at that long-empty storefront, Berkeley’s famed Cheese Board Collective is finally spreading out. The worker-owned institution is taking over the space next door and will run a temporary shipping-container shop on Shattuck while crews rebuild the bakery and cheese counter. The pizzeria is already back in action this week, but the bakery side will soon move into the container as construction ramps up. Collective members say the future layout should feel far less claustrophobic and give them room to offer more cheeses and baked goods. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
